WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.734
A package is the next level of

00:00:01.761 --> 00:00:05.171
organization above a module Remember that a

00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.592
module is usually one Python file A

00:00:08.618 --> 00:00:10.671
package is usually a folder that groups

00:00:10.697 --> 00:00:14.632
related Python modules together Imagine that you

00:00:14.658 --> 00:00:18.013
are building a larger analytics project You

00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:20.539
might have one module for finance calculations

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.658
one module for health-related calculations and one

00:00:23.684 --> 00:00:27.013
module for reporting tools Instead of leaving

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:28.395
all of those files loose in the

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:30.474
main project folder you can group them

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.526
inside a package folder This makes the

00:00:33.553 --> 00:00:37.487
project structure easier to understand When someone

00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:39.526
looks at the folder they can immediately

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:43.566
see which files belong together Traditionally Python

00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:45.829
packages often contain a special file named

00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:48.066
dunder init dot P Y Modern Python

00:00:48.092 --> 00:00:50.303
can support some package structures without that

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:52.145
file but you will still see dunder

00:00:52.158 --> 00:00:53.763
init dot P Y in many real

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:57.355
projects For this introductory module you do

00:00:57.368 --> 00:00:59.618
not need to build a complicated package

00:01:00.553 --> 00:01:02.382
The main goal is to understand the

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:06.118
hierarchy A module is generally one file

00:01:07.039 --> 00:01:08.934
A package is a folder of related

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:12.329
modules A library is a broader collection

00:01:12.355 --> 00:01:14.816
of reusable tools that may contain multiple

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:18.092
packages and modules Later when we use

00:01:18.118 --> 00:01:20.711
libraries such as NumPy and Pandas this

00:01:20.724 --> 00:01:22.842
terminology will make more sense because you

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.816
will see how large collections of Python

00:01:24.842 --> 00:01:25.921
tools are organized
